From: guillermo <guillermo.karsz@solid-run.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 12:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] leds: lp55xx: set the chip pointer before registering the LED class device

lp55xx_register_leds() registers each LED (lp55xx_init_led ->
devm_led_classdev_register) and assigns led->chip only afterwards. With a
default trigger in the device tree (linux,default-trigger = "default-on") the
LED core sets the brightness during registration, lp55xx_set_brightness()
reads led->chip->cfg from a NULL pointer and the kernel oopses at boot
(seen on the HummingBoard IIoT, LP5562, kernel 5.15.32). Assign the pointer
first.

Signed-off-by: guillermo <guillermo.karsz@solid-run.com>
---
--- a/drivers/leds/leds-lp55xx-common.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/leds-lp55xx-common.c
@@ -513,12 +513,18 @@
 
 		led_current = pdata->led_config[i].led_current;
 		each = led + i;
+		/*
+		 * The chip pointer must be valid before the LED class device is
+		 * registered: a default trigger ("linux,default-trigger") sets the
+		 * brightness during registration, and lp55xx_set_brightness()
+		 * dereferences led->chip.
+		 */
+		each->chip = chip;
 		ret = lp55xx_init_led(each, chip, i);
 		if (ret)
 			goto err_init_led;
 
 		chip->num_leds++;
-		each->chip = chip;
 
 		/* setting led current at each channel */
 		if (cfg->set_led_current)
